,"toughness":"3","type_line":"Legendary Creature \u2014 Mutant Warlock Hero"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A boast ability can be activated at any point after the creature with that ability has been declared as an attacker. This can be before blockers are declared, after blockers are declared but before combat damage is dealt, during combat after combat damage is dealt, during the postcombat main phase, during the end step, or, in some unusual cases, during the cleanup step.","oracle_id":"06b77a80-4968-4385-960a-fb66bb4faa94","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature with a boast ability is put onto the battlefield attacking, it was never declared as an attacker. Its boast ability can't be activated that turn.","oracle_id":"06b77a80-4968-4385-960a-fb66bb4faa94","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect adds additional combat phases to a turn and a creature with a boast ability attacks more than once during that turn, its boast ability can still be activated only once.","oracle_id":"06b77a80-4968-4385-960a-fb66bb4faa94","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If it's not your turn and you gain control of a creature with a boast ability after that creature attacked, you can activate that creature's boast ability if it hasn't been activated yet that turn.","oracle_id":"06b77a80-4968-4385-960a-fb66bb4faa94","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Once you announce that you're activating a boast ability, no player may take actions until the ability has been paid for. Notably, opponents can't try to change the activation cost by removing your Dragons.","oracle_id":"06b77a80-4968-4385-960a-fb66bb4faa94","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The cost reduction applies only to generic mana in the activation costs of boast abilities you activate. It can't reduce requirements of specific colors of mana.","oracle_id":"06b77a80-4968-4385-960a-fb66bb4faa94","published_at":"2021-02-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Activated abilities contain a colon. They\u2019re generally written \u201c[Cost]: [Effect].\u201d Some keywords are activated abilities and will have colons in their reminder text.","oracle_id":"81728b98-8cf9-4734-a318-69184bb4d15c","published_at":"2016-06-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature that is equipped is considered modified no matter who controls the Equipment that's attached to it.","oracle_id":"9e0461e7-ccc4-413b-be80-83311be46861","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature with a counter on it is considered modified no matter what kind of counter it is or which player put it on that creature.","oracle_id":"9e0461e7-ccc4-413b-be80-83311be46861","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"All costs to cast a spell are locked in before mana abilities are activated and those costs are paid. If Golden-Tail Trainer's power changes after costs are locked in, or if Golden-Tail Trainer leaves the battlefield while you are activating mana abilities or paying those costs, the cost reduction effect won't be affected and the total cost to cast the spell won't change.","oracle_id":"9e0461e7-ccc4-413b-be80-83311be46861","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An Aura controlled by another player does not cause a creature you control to be modified.","oracle_id":"9e0461e7-ccc4-413b-be80-83311be46861","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The value of X in Golden-Tail Trainer's last ability is determined only as the ability resolves.","oracle_id":"9e0461e7-ccc4-413b-be80-83311be46861","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell remains unchanged, no matter what the total cost to cast it was.","oracle_id":"9e0461e7-ccc4-413b-be80-83311be46861","published_at":"2024-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature enters the battlefield under your control and gains haste, but then loses it before attacking, it won't be able to attack that turn. This means that you can't use one Lightning Greaves to allow two new creatures to attack in the same turn.","oracle_id":"ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't simply unequip Equipment from a creature. If Lightning Greaves is attached to the only creature you control, you won't be able to attach other equipment to it (or target it with anything else) until you have another creature to which you can attach Lightning Greaves.","oracle_id":"ca204b66-8d0c-431a-8d34-282f7c2d17da","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The second ability triggers and resolves during the declare attackers step. The target permanent will be destroyed before blockers are declared.","oracle_id":"d0a1f39b-cda4-4925-83f8-2161f575edfb","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may target any permanent with the triggered ability, not just one controlled by the defending player. If no other player controls a permanent, you must target one of your own.","oracle_id":"d0a1f39b-cda4-4925-83f8-2161f575edfb","published_at":"2011-01-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Activated abilities contain a colon. They're generally written \"[Cost]: [Effect].\" Some keyword abilities are activated abilities and will have colons in their reminder text. Triggered abilities (starting with \"when,\" \"whenever,\" or \"at\") are unaffected by the cost reduction ability of Agatha of the Vile Cauldron.","oracle_id":"f398d222-f8e7-4983-9a77-267adef7f551","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Agatha of the Vile Cauldron's first ability affects only abilities of creatures you control on the battlefield. The costs of activated abilities of creature cards that work in other zones (such as cycling) won't be reduced.","oracle_id":"f398d222-f8e7-4983-9a77-267adef7f551","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
